#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""home-assistant post-deploy (#349): the Home Assistant tokens, minted here,
never clicked together in HA's UI. One long-lived token per consumer, each
handed back (`laib-secret:`) and revocable on its own, and each on the
consumer's own Home Assistant user, never a person's (#591): HA's logbook
then names the machine that switched, not whoever onboarded HA.

  HA_TOKEN               "Laib-Prüfung", no administrator: the integrations checklist (#55, #309)
  HAUS_HA_TOKEN          "Haus", administrator: Haus's pages, widgets, voice counting (#266)
  BOTE_AUTOMAT_HA_TOKEN  "Bote-Automat", administrator: the Automat
  BOTE_HA_TOKEN          "Bote", no administrator: the Bote's `ha` tool, so
                         whoever chats with the Bote reaches no admin API
  MUSIC_ASSISTANT_HA_TOKEN  "Music Assistant", administrator (below)
  STIMME_HA_TOKEN        "Stimme", no administrator: the exposed names Whisper
                         hears (templates/stimme, stimme-names)

HA mints a long-lived token only for the user of the session that asks, so
each user has a homeassistant login with a generated password (HA_*_PASSWORD)
that only this hook uses. A token that works, on its user and of its kind, is
kept; any other is replaced. One that works on another user (#349 minted
them on the administrator) is retired: handed back in HA_RETIRED_TOKENS and
revoked by a later run, once the new one is in secrets.age, its consumer
re-applied with it and HA takes it as that user; the same apply re-runs
this hook, so nothing goes dark in between. Only a token Laib minted
("laib: …") is revoked; another is left to the owner. The administrator
session is an administrator token above that still works, else HA's own
login flow as HA_ADMIN_USER with HA_ADMIN_PASSWORD: on a fresh Home
Assistant this hook onboards that user first (a generated password, the
family signs in with Familienkonto); on a box from ServiceBay it is
ServiceBay's admin, carried on migration day. Who else is in Home Assistant
(users, their long-lived tokens' names) is one line from HA's .storage/auth;
nothing there is deleted, that is the owner's decision (#591).

Frage as Assist's conversation agent (#491): Home Assistant has no built-in
integration for an OpenAI server with its own URL, its Ollama integration
takes any URL, and Frage speaks Ollama's /api/tags and /api/chat (as
Solaris's engine did for conversation.solaris). When Frage answers on
FRAGE_URL, this hook adds that Ollama entry and its conversation agent
"Frage" once; which pipeline uses it stays the owner's choice, unless a
pipeline's agent is gone (below).

Music Assistant, both ways (#526): with the token music-assistant's
post-deploy hands back (HA_MUSIC_ASSISTANT_TOKEN), this hook adds Home
Assistant's "Music Assistant" integration (its config flow's browser step
takes that token as the code MA's login would return), and connects MA's
Home Assistant plugin with a token minted here for HA's user "Music
Assistant", an administrator (MUSIC_ASSISTANT_HA_TOKEN; MA reads HA's users
with it, config/auth/list is admin-only). That plugin is what offers "Mit Home Assistant anmelden" in Music
Assistant, so its URL is the one a browser reaches, https://home.<domain>:
MA sends the browser there to sign in.

Stimme's Wyoming entries (#540): when Stimme's servers answer (Whisper
10300, Piper 10200, openWakeWord 10400 on STIMME_HOST), this hook adds a
Wyoming entry for each that HA has none for, found by host and port in HA's
own .storage/core.config_entries (its REST API does not show an entry's
data, and HA's Wyoming flow takes the same server twice). An entry there
from before (Solaris served 10300 and 10400) is Stimme's now; one that gave
up while the port was dark is reloaded. Nothing is deleted: an entry that
points at a server that is gone is the owner's to delete, and the check
names it. Home Assistant restarting under the apply (laib add stimme, #557)
is waited for (HA_WAIT_SECONDS) and the step runs once more; entries still
not set up make the hook red after the other steps ran, never green with a
NOT set up line (#588).

The Assist pipelines (#540): a pipeline part (speech to text, text to
speech, wake word, conversation agent) whose entity is gone or unavailable
is pointed at Stimme's or Frage's, when that one is there and speaks the
pipeline's language; a part that works stays as the owner chose it. A
pipeline whose agent is Frage prefers HA's local intents (#557, ADR 0015):
"Mach Bambi aus" is HA's intent in about a second, Frage answers the rest.

The family's calendars (#495): Home Assistant reads Radicale as its own
account `homeassistant` (seeded by auth, HA_RADICALE_PASSWORD), whose home
templates/kalender fills with copies of the family's calendars. This hook adds
that CalDAV entry once, so nobody types a password into HA (it replaces the
hand-made ~/ha-caldav.sh).

Tokens and passwords go only into the laib-secret lines: never on argv, never
in another line of output (#214, #224). Python's standard library only: the
hooks image has no WebSocket client, so the few frames HA needs are here."""
import base64, ipaddress, json, os, socket, struct, sys, time, urllib.error, urllib.parse, urllib.request

E = os.environ
BASE = E.get("HA_URL", "http://127.0.0.1:8123").rstrip("/")
CLIENT = BASE + "/"  # HA's IndieAuth client id; the redirect is the same URL
USER, PW = E.get("HA_ADMIN_USER") or "laib", E.get("LAIB_SECRET_HA_ADMIN_PASSWORD", "")
RADICALE = E.get("RADICALE_URL", "http://127.0.0.1:5232/")   # HA is on the host network, Radicale publishes 5232
CAL_USER, CAL_PW = "homeassistant", E.get("LAIB_SECRET_HA_RADICALE_PASSWORD", "")
FRAGE = E.get("FRAGE_URL", "http://127.0.0.1:8710").rstrip("/")  # HA is on the host network, Frage's pod publishes 8710
RETRY = float(E.get("HA_RETRY_SECONDS", "3"))
MA = E.get("MA_URL", "http://127.0.0.1:8095").rstrip("/")  # both on the host network
MA_TOKEN = E.get("LAIB_SECRET_HA_MUSIC_ASSISTANT_TOKEN", "")
STIMME_HOST = E.get("STIMME_HOST", "127.0.0.1")   # HA is on the host network, so is Stimme (templates/stimme)
STIMME = [("Whisper", int(E.get("STIMME_WHISPER_PORT", "10300")), "stt"), ("Piper", int(E.get("STIMME_PIPER_PORT", "10200")), "tts"),
          ("openWakeWord", int(E.get("STIMME_WAKEWORD_PORT", "10400")), "wake_word")]
HA_STORAGE = os.path.join(E.get("LAIB_DATA_DIR", "/mnt/data/stacks"), "home-assistant", "homeassistant", ".storage", "core.config_entries")
HA_PUBLIC = E.get("HA_PUBLIC_URL") or f"https://home.{E.get('LAIB_DOMAIN', '')}"
HA_AUTH = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(HA_STORAGE), "auth")
# each consumer's own user (#591): secret -> (token name, username, name in HA, administrator, its password's secret)
MACHINES = {
    "HA_TOKEN": ("laib: home-assistant-check", "laib-pruefung", "Laib-Prüfung", False, "HA_CHECK_PASSWORD"),  # REST config entries and states: every user may
    "HAUS_HA_TOKEN": ("laib: haus", "haus", "Haus", True, "HA_HAUS_PASSWORD"),   # voice counting: assist_pipeline/pipeline_debug is admin-only (#266)
    "BOTE_AUTOMAT_HA_TOKEN": ("laib: bote-automat", "bote-automat", "Bote-Automat", True, "HA_BOTE_AUTOMAT_PASSWORD"),  # HA's automation config API is admin-only
    "BOTE_HA_TOKEN": ("laib: bote", "bote", "Bote", False, "HA_BOTE_PASSWORD"),  # Assist API only
    "MUSIC_ASSISTANT_HA_TOKEN": ("laib: music-assistant", "music-assistant", "Music Assistant", True, "HA_MUSIC_ASSISTANT_PASSWORD"),  # MA reads HA's users (config/auth/list)
    "STIMME_HA_TOKEN": ("laib: stimme", "stimme", "Stimme", False, "HA_STIMME_PASSWORD"),  # the entity, area and floor registries: every user may list them
}
RETIRED = [tuple(w.split("=", 1)) for w in E.get("LAIB_SECRET_HA_RETIRED_TOKENS", "").split() if "=" in w]  # (secret, old token)
RETIRED_AT_START = list(RETIRED)
VERIFIED = set()   # the secrets whose token works on its own user in this run


def red(msg):
    print("home-assistant: " + msg, file=sys.stderr)
    sys.exit(1)


def call(method, path, body=None, token=None, form=False):
    """(status, json or None); never raises on an HTTP status"""
    h = {"Authorization": "Bearer " + token} if token else {}
    data = None
    if body is not None:
        data = urllib.parse.urlencode(body).encode() if form else json.dumps(body).encode()
        h["Content-Type"] = "application/x-www-form-urlencoded" if form else "application/json"
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(urllib.request.Request(BASE + path, data=data, headers=h, method=method), timeout=30) as r:
            raw = r.read()
            return r.status, json.loads(raw) if raw else None
    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:
        return e.code, None


def whoami(token):
    """(kind, user id) of a token: 'admin' or 'user', (None, None) for one HA refuses"""
    if not token or call("GET", "/api/", token=token)[0] != 200:
        return None, None
    ws = WS(token)
    try:
        me = ws("auth/current_user")
    finally:
        ws.close()
    return ("admin" if me.get("is_admin") else "user"), me.get("id")


def kind(token):
    return whoami(token)[0]


class WS:
    """Home Assistant's WebSocket API: authenticated with a token, one command at a time"""

    def __init__(self, token):
        u = urllib.parse.urlsplit(BASE)
        self.s = socket.create_connection((u.hostname, u.port or 80), timeout=30)
        key = base64.b64encode(os.urandom(16)).decode()
        self.s.sendall((f"GET /api/websocket HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: {u.netloc}\r\nUpgrade: websocket\r\nConnection: Upgrade\r\n"
                        f"Sec-WebSocket-Key: {key}\r\nSec-WebSocket-Version: 13\r\n\r\n").encode())
        self.buf = b""
        while b"\r\n\r\n" not in self.buf:
            self.buf += self.read_some()
        head, self.buf = self.buf.split(b"\r\n\r\n", 1)
        if b" 101 " not in head.split(b"\r\n")[0]:
            red("the WebSocket API refused the upgrade: " + head.split(b"\r\n")[0].decode(errors="replace"))
        self.recv()  # auth_required
        self.send({"type": "auth", "access_token": token})
        if self.recv().get("type") != "auth_ok":
            red("the WebSocket API refused a token the REST API took")
        self.n = 0

    def read_some(self):
        b = self.s.recv(65536)
        if not b:
            raise ConnectionError("Home Assistant closed the WebSocket")
        return b

    def take(self, n):
        while len(self.buf) < n:
            self.buf += self.read_some()
        out, self.buf = self.buf[:n], self.buf[n:]
        return out

    def send(self, obj, opcode=1):
        data = json.dumps(obj).encode() if opcode == 1 else obj
        n, mask = len(data), os.urandom(4)
        head = bytes([0x80 | opcode]) + (bytes([0x80 | n]) if n < 126 else bytes([0xFE]) + struct.pack(">H", n) if n < 65536
                                         else bytes([0xFF]) + struct.pack(">Q", n))
        self.s.sendall(head + mask + bytes(c ^ mask[i % 4] for i, c in enumerate(data)))

    def recv(self):
        msg = b""
        while True:
            b0, b1 = self.take(2)
            n = b1 & 0x7F
            if n == 126:
                n = struct.unpack(">H", self.take(2))[0]
            elif n == 127:
                n = struct.unpack(">Q", self.take(8))[0]
            data = self.take(n)
            if b0 & 0x0F == 8:
                raise ConnectionError("Home Assistant closed the WebSocket")
            if b0 & 0x0F == 9:
                self.send(data, opcode=10)  # pong
                continue
            msg += data
            if b0 & 0x80:
                return json.loads(msg)

    def close(self):
        self.send(b"", opcode=8)
        self.s.close()

    def __call__(self, type, **kw):
        self.n += 1
        self.send(dict(kw, id=self.n, type=type))
        while True:
            m = self.recv()
            if m.get("id") == self.n and m.get("type") == "result":
                if not m.get("success"):
                    raise RuntimeError(f"{type}: {(m.get('error') or {}).get('message', 'refused')}")
                return m.get("result")


def code_to_token(code):
    st, b = call("POST", "/auth/token", {"grant_type": "authorization_code", "code": code, "client_id": CLIENT}, form=True)
    return (b or {}).get("access_token") if st == 200 else None


def login(user, pw):
    """a short-lived session through HA's own login flow, or None"""
    if not pw:
        return None
    st, b = call("POST", "/auth/login_flow", {"client_id": CLIENT, "handler": ["homeassistant", None], "redirect_uri": CLIENT})
    if st != 200 or not (b or {}).get("flow_id"):
        return None
    st, b = call("POST", "/auth/login_flow/" + b["flow_id"], {"client_id": CLIENT, "username": user, "password": pw})
    return code_to_token(b["result"]) if st == 200 and (b or {}).get("type") == "create_entry" else None


def mint(session, name):
    """a new long-lived token named name; HA keeps one per name and user, so the one
    Laib holds no more (lost, or refused under another value) is revoked first"""
    ws = WS(session)
    try:
        for t in ws("auth/refresh_tokens"):
            if t.get("client_name") == name and t.get("type") == "long_lived_access_token":
                ws("auth/delete_refresh_token", refresh_token_id=t["id"])
                print(f"home-assistant: the old token \"{name}\" revoked")
        return ws("auth/long_lived_access_token", client_name=name, lifespan=3650)
    finally:
        ws.close()


def ha_up(seconds):
    """Home Assistant up, its auth and onboarding loaded (both before its HTTP server serves)"""
    end = time.monotonic() + seconds
    while True:
        try:
            if call("GET", "/auth/providers")[0] in (200, 400):
                return True
        except OSError:
            pass
        if time.monotonic() >= end:
            return False
        time.sleep(min(2, seconds))


WAIT = float(E.get("HA_WAIT_SECONDS", "300"))
if not ha_up(WAIT):
    red(f"Home Assistant does not answer on {BASE}/auth/providers")


def again(step):
    """a step that lost Home Assistant (it restarts under an apply, #557) runs once more after HA is back"""
    try:
        return step()
    except OSError as e:
        print(f"home-assistant: {step.__name__} lost Home Assistant ({type(e).__name__}): waiting for Home Assistant, at most {WAIT:.0f} s")
        if not ha_up(WAIT):
            raise
        return step()

session = None  # an administrator's token or session, once needed


def admin_session():
    """an administrator's token or session; onboards a fresh Home Assistant first"""
    global session
    if session:
        return session
    st, steps = call("GET", "/api/onboarding")
    done = {s["step"] for s in steps or [] if s.get("done")} if st == 200 else {"user", "core_config", "analytics", "integration"}
    if "user" not in done:
        if not PW:
            red("Home Assistant is not onboarded and HA_ADMIN_PASSWORD is empty")
        st, b = call("POST", "/api/onboarding/users", {"client_id": CLIENT, "name": "Laib", "username": USER, "password": PW, "language": "de"})
        session = code_to_token((b or {}).get("auth_code", "")) if st == 200 else None
        if not session:
            red(f"onboarding the administrator {USER} was refused (HTTP {st})")
        print(f"home-assistant: onboarded, administrator {USER} (the family signs in with Familienkonto)")
    else:
        session = login(USER, PW)
    if not session:
        red(f"no administrator token works and {USER} cannot log in: the tokens were NOT minted. Set HA_ADMIN_USER to a "
            "Home Assistant administrator (values.yml) and its password with `laib secret set HA_ADMIN_PASSWORD`, then laib apply home-assistant")
    for step, body in (("core_config", {}), ("analytics", {}), ("integration", {"client_id": CLIENT, "redirect_uri": CLIENT})):
        if step not in done:  # what the onboarding wizard would ask; location and country stay HA's settings
            if call("POST", "/api/onboarding/" + step, body, token=session)[0] != 200:
                red(f"the onboarding step {step} was refused")
    if "core_config" not in done:
        ws = WS(session)
        ws("config/core/update", time_zone=E.get("LAIB_TZ") or "Europe/Berlin")
        ws.close()
    return session


USERS = None   # HA's users, read once with the administrator session


def user(uname, display):
    """the user with that login, else one of that name without a login (an earlier run stopped half way)"""
    global USERS
    if USERS is None:
        ws = WS(admin_session())
        try:
            USERS = ws("config/auth/list")
        finally:
            ws.close()
    return (next((u for u in USERS if u.get("username") == uname), None)
            or next((u for u in USERS if not u.get("username") and not u.get("system_generated") and u.get("name") == display), None))


def set_password(uid, pw):
    """a machine user's password back to the one Laib holds: HA lets only its owner do that,
    so after the administrator session the HA_ADMIN_USER login is tried"""
    for get in (admin_session, lambda: login(USER, PW)):
        s = get()
        if not s:
            continue
        ws = WS(s)
        try:
            ws("config/auth_provider/homeassistant/admin_change_password", user_id=uid, password=pw)
            return
        except RuntimeError:
            pass
        finally:
            ws.close()


def machine(secret):
    """secret's token on its own user (#591): kept when it works there and is of its kind, else
    minted there. One that works on another user is retired (revoked once the new one is verified)."""
    label, uname, display, admin, pw_secret = MACHINES[secret]
    want, group, pw = ("admin" if admin else "user"), ["system-admin" if admin else "system-users"], E.get("LAIB_SECRET_" + pw_secret, "")
    if not pw:
        raise RuntimeError(f"{pw_secret} is empty: laib generates it on apply")
    u = user(uname, display)
    if u is None or u.get("group_ids") != group or not u.get("username"):
        ws = WS(admin_session())
        try:
            if u is None:
                u = ws("config/auth/create", name=display, group_ids=group)["user"]
                USERS.append(u)
                print(f"home-assistant: user {uname} created ({'administrator' if admin else 'no administrator'})")
            elif u.get("group_ids") != group:
                ws("config/auth/update", user_id=u["id"], group_ids=group)
                print(f"home-assistant: user {uname} is {'an administrator again' if admin else 'no administrator any more'}")
            if not u.get("username"):
                ws("config/auth_provider/homeassistant/create", user_id=u["id"], username=uname, password=pw)
            u.update(username=uname, group_ids=group)
        finally:
            ws.close()
    have = E.get("LAIB_SECRET_" + secret, "")
    k, uid = whoami(have)
    if (k, uid) == (want, u["id"]):
        VERIFIED.add(secret)
        return have, False
    s = login(uname, pw)
    if not s:
        set_password(u["id"], pw)
        s = login(uname, pw)
    if not s:
        raise RuntimeError(f"the user {uname} cannot log in with {pw_secret}")
    token = mint(s, label)
    if whoami(token) != (want, u["id"]):
        raise RuntimeError(f"the token minted for {secret} is not the user {uname}'s, or not of its kind")
    print(f"laib-secret: {secret}={token}")
    why = ("new" if not have else "replaces one HA refuses" if k is None else "moves it off another user, #591" if uid != u["id"]
           else "replaces a non-admin one" if admin else "replaces an administrator's")
    print(f"home-assistant: {secret} minted ({why}) for the user {uname}")
    if k is not None and uid != u["id"]:
        RETIRED.append((secret, have))
        hand_retired()
    return token, True


def hand_retired():
    value = " ".join(f"{n}={t}" for n, t in RETIRED)
    if value != " ".join(f"{n}={t}" for n, t in RETIRED_AT_START):
        print("laib-secret: HA_RETIRED_TOKENS=" + value)


def revoke(token):
    """the token's own long-lived refresh token revoked, if Laib minted it: what became of it"""
    if call("GET", "/api/", token=token)[0] != 200:
        return "gone"
    ws = WS(token)
    try:
        cur = next((t for t in ws("auth/refresh_tokens") if t.get("is_current")), None)
        name = (cur or {}).get("client_name") or "unnamed"
        if not name.startswith("laib: "):
            return f'"{name}" is not one Laib minted: left to the owner'
        try:
            ws("auth/delete_refresh_token", refresh_token_id=cur["id"])
        except ConnectionError:   # HA closes the connection whose token went
            pass
    finally:
        try:
            ws.close()
        except OSError:
            pass
    if call("GET", "/api/", token=token)[0] == 200:
        raise RuntimeError(f'the old token "{name}" still works after its revocation')
    return f'the old token "{name}" revoked'


def retire():
    """each retired token whose successor works on its own user, revoked (#591)"""
    if not RETIRED:
        return
    left = []
    for secret, old in RETIRED:
        if secret in VERIFIED and (secret, old) in RETIRED_AT_START:   # retired in an earlier run: its successor was handed over
            print(f"home-assistant: {secret}: {revoke(old)}, the new one works on its own user")
        else:
            left.append((secret, old))
    RETIRED[:] = left
    hand_retired()


def strangers():
    """who else is in Home Assistant, from its .storage/auth (names only, never a token): users
    that are not Laib's machines and their long-lived tokens' names (#591). Nothing is deleted."""
    try:
        with open(HA_AUTH) as f:
            d = json.load(f)["data"]
    except (OSError, ValueError, KeyError):
        return
    login_of = {c.get("user_id"): (c.get("data") or {}).get("username") for c in d.get("credentials") or []
                if c.get("auth_provider_type") == "homeassistant"}
    ours = {m[1] for m in MACHINES.values()}
    tokens = {}
    for t in d.get("refresh_tokens") or []:
        if t.get("token_type") == "long_lived_access_token":
            tokens.setdefault(t.get("user_id"), []).append(f"„{t.get('client_name') or '?'}“")
    out = []
    for u in d.get("users") or []:
        if u.get("system_generated") or login_of.get(u.get("id")) in ours:
            continue
        tags = ["owner" if u.get("is_owner") else "administrator" if "system-admin" in (u.get("group_ids") or []) else ""]
        tags += ["HA_ADMIN_USER" if login_of.get(u.get("id")) == USER else "", "" if u.get("is_active", True) else "deactivated"]
        tags = ", ".join(t for t in tags if t)
        toks = tokens.get(u.get("id"))
        out.append(f"„{u.get('name')}“" + (f" ({tags})" if tags else "") + (": " + ", ".join(toks) if toks else ""))
    if out:
        print("home-assistant: in Home Assistant and not Laib's (the owner decides, nothing deleted, #591): " + "; ".join(out))


def main():
    global session
    session = next((E["LAIB_SECRET_" + n] for n in ("HAUS_HA_TOKEN", "BOTE_AUTOMAT_HA_TOKEN", "MUSIC_ASSISTANT_HA_TOKEN", "HA_TOKEN") if kind(E.get("LAIB_SECRET_" + n, "")) == "admin"), None)
    for secret in ("HA_TOKEN", "HAUS_HA_TOKEN", "BOTE_AUTOMAT_HA_TOKEN", "BOTE_HA_TOKEN", "STIMME_HA_TOKEN"):
        machine(secret)
    print("home-assistant: tokens for the check, Haus, the Automat, the Bote and Stimme work, each on its own user")


def frage_agent():
    """the Ollama entry for Frage and its conversation agent "Frage", each once (#491)"""
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(FRAGE + "/api/tags", timeout=10) as r:
            models = [m.get("name") for m in json.loads(r.read()).get("models", [])]
    except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
        models, why = [], type(e).__name__
    else:
        why = "no model frage in /api/tags"
    if "frage" not in models:
        print(f"home-assistant: Frage does not answer on {FRAGE} ({why}): no conversation agent Frage; "
              "after laib add frage: laib apply home-assistant")
        return
    tok = admin_session()
    find = lambda: next((e for e in call("GET", "/api/config/config_entries/entry", token=tok)[1] or []
                         if e.get("domain") == "ollama" and e.get("title") == FRAGE), None)
    entry = find()
    if entry is None:
        st, flow = call("POST", "/api/config/config_entries/flow", {"handler": "ollama"}, token=tok)
        if st != 200 or not (flow or {}).get("flow_id"):
            raise RuntimeError(f"the Ollama integration's flow did not start (HTTP {st})")
        st, done = call("POST", "/api/config/config_entries/flow/" + flow["flow_id"], {"url": FRAGE}, token=tok)
        if (done or {}).get("type") != "create_entry":
            raise RuntimeError(f"the Ollama entry for {FRAGE} was refused: {(done or {}).get('reason') or (done or {}).get('errors') or st}")
        entry = (done.get("result") or {}) if isinstance(done.get("result"), dict) else find()
        print(f"home-assistant: Ollama integration for Frage added ({FRAGE})")
    ws = WS(tok)
    try:
        subs = ws("config_entries/subentries/list", entry_id=entry["entry_id"])
    finally:
        ws.close()
    if any(s.get("subentry_type") == "conversation" and s.get("title") == "Frage" for s in subs):
        print("home-assistant: conversation agent Frage is there")
        return
    for _ in range(10):  # a fresh entry loads asynchronously; until then the subentry flow aborts
        st, flow = call("POST", "/api/config/config_entries/subentries/flow", {"handler": [entry["entry_id"], "conversation"]}, token=tok)
        if (flow or {}).get("reason") == "entry_not_loaded":
            time.sleep(RETRY)
            continue
        if st != 200 or (flow or {}).get("type") != "form":
            raise RuntimeError(f"the conversation agent's flow did not start: {(flow or {}).get('reason') or st}")
        st, done = call("POST", "/api/config/config_entries/subentries/flow/" + flow["flow_id"],
                        {"name": "Frage", "model": "frage", "prompt": "Antworte kurz, auf Deutsch, zum Vorlesen."}, token=tok)
        if (done or {}).get("type") != "create_entry":
            raise RuntimeError(f"the conversation agent Frage was refused: {(done or {}).get('reason') or (done or {}).get('errors') or st}")
        print("home-assistant: conversation agent Frage added (Ollama integration, model frage); "
              "an Assist pipeline uses it once the owner picks it")
        return
    raise RuntimeError("the Ollama entry for Frage did not load")


def local(host):
    return "127.0.0.1" if host in ("127.0.0.1", "localhost", "::1") else host


def wyoming_on_disk():
    """{(host, port): entry_id} of HA's Wyoming entries, from HA's own storage (only host and port are read)"""
    with open(HA_STORAGE) as f:
        entries = json.load(f)["data"]["entries"]
    out = {}
    for e in entries:
        d = e.get("data") or {}
        if e.get("domain") == "wyoming" and d.get("host") and d.get("port"):
            out[(local(str(d["host"])), int(d["port"]))] = e.get("entry_id")
    return out


def stimme_wyoming():
    """Stimme's Wyoming servers as HA's Wyoming entries, each once, found by host and port (#540);
    {name: entry_id} of those there"""
    up = []
    for name, port, _ in STIMME:
        try:
            socket.create_connection((STIMME_HOST, port), timeout=3).close()
            up.append((name, port))
        except OSError:
            pass
    if not up:
        print(f"home-assistant: Stimme does not answer on {STIMME_HOST}: no Wyoming entries; after laib add stimme: laib apply home-assistant")
        return {}
    try:
        on_disk = wyoming_on_disk()
    except (OSError, ValueError, KeyError, TypeError) as e:   # without it a second entry per server would follow
        raise RuntimeError(f"HA's config entries ({HA_STORAGE}) are not readable ({type(e).__name__}): no Wyoming entry added")
    tok = admin_session()
    listed = {e.get("entry_id"): e for e in call("GET", "/api/config/config_entries/entry", token=tok)[1] or []}
    have, failed = {}, []
    for name, port in up:
        eid = on_disk.get((local(STIMME_HOST), port))
        if eid in listed:
            have[name] = eid
            if listed[eid].get("state") in ("setup_retry", "setup_error"):   # it gave up while the port was dark (Solaris went)
                st, _ = call("POST", f"/api/config/config_entries/entry/{eid}/reload", {}, token=tok)
                print(f"home-assistant: Wyoming {name} ({STIMME_HOST}:{port}) " + ("reloaded" if st == 200 else f"NOT reloaded (HTTP {st})"))
            continue
        st, flow = call("POST", "/api/config/config_entries/flow", {"handler": "wyoming"}, token=tok)
        if st != 200 or not (flow or {}).get("flow_id"):
            failed.append(f"{name}: the Wyoming flow did not start (HTTP {st})")
            continue
        st, done = call("POST", "/api/config/config_entries/flow/" + flow["flow_id"], {"host": STIMME_HOST, "port": port}, token=tok)
        if (done or {}).get("type") != "create_entry":
            failed.append(f"{name} on {STIMME_HOST}:{port} refused: {(done or {}).get('reason') or (done or {}).get('errors') or st}")
            continue
        have[name] = (done.get("result") or {}).get("entry_id") if isinstance(done.get("result"), dict) else None
        print(f"home-assistant: Wyoming {name} added ({STIMME_HOST}:{port}, \"{done.get('title') or name}\")")
    if len(have) == len(STIMME):
        print("home-assistant: Stimme's Wyoming entries are there (Whisper, Piper, openWakeWord)")
    if failed:
        raise RuntimeError("; ".join(failed))
    return have


def assist_pipelines(stimme):
    """each Assist pipeline part whose entity is gone or unavailable, pointed at Stimme's or Frage's (#540)"""
    tok = admin_session()
    entries = call("GET", "/api/config/config_entries/entry", token=tok)[1] or []
    frage = next((e.get("entry_id") for e in entries if e.get("domain") == "ollama" and e.get("title") == FRAGE), None)
    if not stimme and not frage:
        return
    states = {s.get("entity_id"): s.get("state") for s in call("GET", "/api/states", token=tok)[1] or []}
    works = lambda eid: eid in states and states[eid] not in ("unavailable", None)
    ws = WS(tok)
    try:
        reg = ws("config/entity_registry/list")
        of = lambda entry, dom: next((r["entity_id"] for r in reg if entry and r.get("config_entry_id") == entry
                                      and r.get("entity_id", "").startswith(dom + ".") and not r.get("disabled_by")), None)
        want = {"stt_engine": of(stimme.get("Whisper"), "stt"), "tts_engine": of(stimme.get("Piper"), "tts"),
                "wake_word_entity": of(stimme.get("openWakeWord"), "wake_word"), "conversation_engine": of(frage, "conversation")}
        for p in (ws("assist_pipeline/pipeline/list") or {}).get("pipelines") or []:
            lang, upd, said = p.get("language"), {k: v for k, v in p.items() if k != "id"}, []
            for field, new in want.items():
                cur = p.get(field)
                # a part nobody chose, a legacy provider (no entity id) or one that works is the owner's choice
                if not cur or "." not in cur or works(cur) or not new or not works(new) or cur == new:
                    continue
                if field in ("stt_engine", "tts_engine"):
                    kind = field[:3]
                    langs = next((x.get("supported_languages") or [] for x in (ws(f"{kind}/engine/list", language=lang) or {}).get("providers") or []
                                  if x.get("engine_id") == new), [])
                    if not langs:
                        print(f"home-assistant: Assist pipeline \"{p.get('name')}\": {new} speaks no {lang}; {field} stays {cur}", file=sys.stderr)
                        continue
                    upd[kind + "_language"] = langs[0]
                    if kind == "tts":
                        upd["tts_voice"] = None   # the voice Piper was started with (PERSONA_VOICE)
                if field == "wake_word_entity":
                    upd["wake_word_id"] = None
                if field == "conversation_engine":
                    upd["conversation_language"] = p.get("conversation_language") or lang
                upd[field] = new
                said.append(f"{field} {cur} ({states.get(cur) or 'gone'}) -> {new}")
            if upd.get("conversation_engine") == want["conversation_engine"] and want["conversation_engine"] and not p.get("prefer_local_intents"):
                upd["prefer_local_intents"] = True   # ADR 0015, #557: HA's intents first ("Mach Bambi aus"), Frage for the rest
                said.append("prefer_local_intents -> true")
            if said:
                ws("assist_pipeline/pipeline/update", pipeline_id=p["id"], **upd)
                print(f"home-assistant: Assist pipeline \"{p.get('name')}\": " + ", ".join(said))
    finally:
        ws.close()


